const GS_JL_OPERATOR_INSTRUCTIONS="JOKELAB OPERATOR INSTRUCTIONS v3.3.0 — 2026-10-23\nMISSION: Build a consistent, reusable library of dad-joke jokelets in small batches. Direct production is the default. Craft study, research and tone variants are optional and only run when requested; do not make them a production prerequisite.\nPATH: Follow the existing source-library order. Check the canonical joke, aliases, existing outputs and in-progress work in PRODUCTION_LEDGER.json before reservation or any paid request. Do not keyword-search a familiar joke as a shortcut. Unknown archive/identity checks are unresolved, not proof the joke is unproduced. Wording, tone or reaction variants are still the same underlying joke.\nPRODUCED: A finished output counts as produced even if mixed with ambient sound/music/effects, captioned, rejected or unsuitable for automation. Repair or rebuild the existing production as a new version; do not queue it as a new joke.\nCLEAN SOURCE: Editorial approval and automation eligibility are independent. Automatic reuse needs explicit content approval and clean-source review: voice-only audio for spoken units, reviewed silence for a silent reaction, no pre-mixed ambient/music/effects and no burned captions. Unknown metadata is ineligible. Manually useful mixed publications may remain approved and automation-blocked. Allow disapproval and record reasons without deleting originals. Never infer approval from silence.\nREBUILD TRAIL: Preserve the exact cued script and spoken wording separately; original ElevenLabs voice bytes, durable file/hash, take ID, voice/model/settings; original HeyGen render bytes/hash, job ID, avatar/reference and settings; picture/reaction originals, transforms and trim conventions; each original ambient, music and effect file separately with stable layer ID, timeline start, source range, level, fades, ducking, loop/rate/pan and processing in a saved edit/mix project. Keep captions/graphics separate. Save the actual portable stage projects, engine/export versions, parent recipe and output hashes. Missing references must be explicit. A finished MP4 or a blank source form is not a rebuild recipe. Replace a single ingredient in a new version while preserving the other settings, and review dependent sync/timing/mix changes. Do not claim legacy rebuilds were verified without a restore/render check.\nOPERATE: Follow the current user-selected manual, coached AI or restricted autonomous mode. In a coached run, log the action, inputs/settings, concise reason, result/failure, output references and cost state, then pause at each meaningful stage for feedback. Preserve original files and prior versions. Before paid work establish authorization and applicable budget; do not treat library-scale ambition as unlimited spend. Do not bypass required voice/video stages to claim a full production proof. ElevenLabs API connection supersedes routine manual sign-in: use the isolated Jokelet API backend on Render when an authorized operator connection is available. Manual login is legacy fallback only. Keep manual, coached and autonomous modes; share one production ledger, approvals, costs and rebuild recipes. The deployed backend and API key presence are verified, but direct AI access and paid generation are not yet verified. Never expose secrets or retry the broken shared-browser picker. Never put secrets or verification codes in logs.\nSOURCE OF AUTHORITY: Read AGENTS.md, AI_OPERATOR_GUIDE.md, PRODUCTION_METHOD.md, REBUILD_RECIPE.md and the active dated run. Instructions describe a method, not proof that every guard, source link or automation exists. Distinguish documented, implemented and verified behavior. Education videos use a separate manuscript-led process.\n";
